  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bogota Subnational Bond</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is expected to improve access to quality urban transport for underserved populations enabling shorter travel times to jobs, educational opportunities and economic inclusionalongside reducing environmental footprint for Bogot&#xe1;&apos;s mass transit system. Beyond the Project, IFC anticipates that its investment will have a demonstration effect and contribute to financial resilience of municipal entities, capital markets integration, and will encourage further placement of sustainable finance instruments in Colombia and Latin America and the Caribbean.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed investment consists of a purchase by IFC, for its own account, of a senior unsecured Colombian peso-linked bond to be issued by Bogot&#xe1; Distrito Capital (Bogot&#xe1; or the Municipality) for an amount of up to US$125 million. IFC proceeds will be used for funding the Municipalitys obligations under the Linea 2 del Metro de Bogot&#xe1; (in English, Bogota Metro Line 2  BML2), being developed by the Bogot&#xe1; Metro Company (EMB).</narrative>
  </description>
